Description: OWASP Core Rule Set 4 for ModSecurity-compatible WAFs
 The OWASP Core Rule Set (CRS) is a set of generic attack detection rules
 for web application firewalls that read ModSecurity's rule language:
 SQL injection, cross-site scripting, local file inclusion, remote code
 execution and other common attacks, scored by anomaly.
 .
 This package holds CRS version 4. The rules are in
 /usr/share/coreruleset/rules, the local settings in /etc/coreruleset, and
 /usr/share/coreruleset/coreruleset.load includes both in CRS's order, for
 example from Coraza's Nginx module. Debian's modsecurity-crs holds the
 older CRS 3.3 for ModSecurity; both can be installed together.
